    <l n="1" type="heading" level="1" caput="1" para="true">DISQVISITIO PRIMA.</l>
    <l n="2" type="heading" level="2" para="true">Quænam sint causæ corruptionis.</l>
    <l n="3" para="true">PRO intelligentia non parum inser-</l>
    <l n="4">uiunt Aristotelis verba 1. Meteor.</l>
    <l n="5">tex. 44. quòd sol dum per Zodiacum</l>
    <l n="6">obliquè mouetur, quia prope fit, aut</l>
    <l n="7">longiùs, dum vel accedit ad Cancrum,</l>
    <l n="8">vel ad Capricornum, causa generatio-</l>
    <l n="9">nis, &amp; corruptionis est. Quippe cum</l>
    <l n="10">huc in terras modò maiores habeat ir-</l>
    <l n="11">radiationes, modò minores, ideoque</l>
    <l n="12">calorem producat diuersum, per hunc</l>
    <l n="13">accessum, recessumque, ait Philosophus,</l>
    <l n="14">vicissitudinem generationis, &amp; corrup-</l>
    <l n="15">tionis facit. Sicut ergo in Chymia ra-</l>
    <l n="16">tio agendi tota in eo sita videtur, vt</l>
    <l n="17">optimum adsit regimen ignis, &amp; appli-</l>
    <l n="18">catio caloris pro materiæ indigentia,</l>
    <l n="19">quæ alterari, disponi, &amp; perfici debet:</l>
    <l n="20">Ita cum sol sit ignis cælestis, natura</l>
    <l n="21">hoc maximè prouidit, vt per accessum,</l>
    <l n="22">&amp; recessum diuersimodè calefaceret,</l>
    <l n="23">materiasque mouendo ministerium age-</l>
    <l n="24">ret generationis, &amp; corruptionis.</l>
    <l n="25" para="true">Calor igitur est prima corruptionis</l>
    <l n="26">causa, nam ille dum recipitur in com-</l>
    <l n="27">posito, humidique particulas afficit plus-</l>
    <l n="28">quam natura vel exigat, vel ferre possit,</l>
    <l n="29">eas cogit recedere intimè atq; à proprio</l>
    <l n="30">centro se remouere. Oritur inde, vt in</l>
    <l n="31">bullas minutissimas colligantur, maio-</l>
    <l n="32">remq; locum petendo, vicinas materiæ</l>
  </main_text>
